The public API is `decode_nonblank(payload, encodings=("utf-8", "latin-1"))`. `payload` must be `bytes`. `encodings` must be a non-empty list or tuple of unique non-empty strings recognized by Python. Decode strictly using each encoding in order until one succeeds. Return a tuple of stripped, non-empty lines, preserving line order. Empty or whitespace-only decoded content returns `()`. If every encoding rejects the bytes, re-raise the `UnicodeDecodeError` from the final attempt. Raise `ValueError` for malformed arguments or unknown encoding names. Do not mutate inputs.

